{# Persistent frame: unchanged on every page, kept mounted by the router. #}
<header class="masthead">
  <div class="container">
    {% include "partials/nav.njk" %}

    <a class="masthead__brand" href="/">
      <img class="masthead__logo logo--spin" src="/assets/images/logo.png" alt="" />
      <img class="masthead__wordmark" src="/assets/images/wordmark.png" alt="{{ site.name }}" />
    </a>

    {# Slogan, parked for now:
    <p class="masthead__title">
      {{ site.slogan.lead }} <span class="text-accent">{{ site.slogan.accent }}</span>
    </p>
    #}

    <p class="lead lead--strong">
      The platform for test development and orchestration<br />
      that lets you and your <strong class="text-agent">AI agents</strong> run the entire testing operation
    </p>
  </div>

  {# The thesis sits on the page background so the home page alternates from the very top. #}
  <div class="masthead__principles">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="pillars" data-reveal-group>
        <article class="pillar reveal">
          <div class="pillar__head">
            <span class="pillar__icon">{% icon "stack-2" %}</span>
            <h3 id="test-suite-standardization" class="pillar__title">Test suite standardization</h3>
          </div>
          <p class="pillar__text">Every suite has the
            <a class="text-accent" href="/framework/#component-model">same structure</a> in plain Python. An AI
            agent writes it with no API to learn; the controller derives the GUI from it.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="pillar reveal">
          <div class="pillar__head">
            <span class="pillar__icon">{% icon "code" %}</span>
            <h3 id="continuous-test-development" class="pillar__title">Continuous test development</h3>
          </div>
          <p class="pillar__text">The suite grows with the system. On demand or on a schedule, the AI agent adds
            the missing tests, and every fixed bug becomes a test.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="pillar reveal">
          <div class="pillar__head">
            <span class="pillar__icon">{% icon "hierarchy" %}</span>
            <h3 id="orchestration" class="pillar__title">Orchestration</h3>
          </div>
          <p class="pillar__text">When asked or when scheduled, the AI agent picks the machines and runs
            <a class="text-accent" href="/setup/">across the lab</a>. The controller ships the package and
            collects the results.</p>
        </article>
        <article class="pillar reveal">
          <div class="pillar__head">
            <span class="pillar__icon">{% icon "infinity" %}</span>
            <h3 id="continuous-integration" class="pillar__title">Continuous integration</h3>
          </div>
          <p class="pillar__text">The same suite runs unattended in the pipeline, from a snapshot exported from
            the GUI or a batch the AI agent writes, with the same results.</p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</header>
